WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:06.519 align:start position:0%
 
whoa  like the spartan sheen of its digital  environments volume is self that it's  most fundamental level  it's a fine-tuned equation and aside  from several threatening variables not  much can upset its balance volume is a  futuristic retelling of the classic  Robin Hood legend it takes place in  simulations filled with labyrinthian  corridors and enemy guards in which our  hero Rob Locksley broadcasts  hypothetical heists against corrupt  corporations there are trip lasers alarm  panels and automated tourists to  traverse it's our job not only to  navigate these hazards but also collect  a certain number of floating gems these  unlock and exit portal place somewhere  in the environment and this puts a  creative twist on the classic stealth  formula imagine Solid Snake of Metal  Gear Fame thrown into pac-man with only  a few gadgets and his bare hands to help  him survive slinking through these  booby-trapped mazes is as much about  careful traversal as patient observation  and observation is important because  volume is just as much a puzzle game as  it is a member of the stealth genre most  levels don't leave room for  improvisation instead guiding you with  visual clues and subtle hints toward the  exit the fun in volume doesn't lie in  choosing your favorite approach but  finally discovering the one that works  volume has a clean simple visual  vocabulary which never leaves anything  open to interpretation it places  function over form and by definition  that's good design guard vision cones  are always visible electrified tiles are  apparent and lasers emit a bright white  streak these lasers can lead to frequent  restarts as your character sometimes  keeps moving after you let go of the  computer key or analog stick but it  didn't happen often enough to prolong  the frustration even volumes audio cues  emit a white circle using these to  manipulate guards is essential and  learning them from their positions is  only a matter of whistling there are  also gadgets to aid in distractions the  white circles are precise and never  leave any doubt as to whether guards  would hear you or not ironic as it is in  a game called volume I could have  finished it with the sound turned off  volume also features simple deep and  accessible editing tools I created  several maps that proved challenging and  it didn't take me long to learn how the  different tools work these levels don't  end up telling the story the campaign  does but I think that's for the better  volume makes an attempt at broad social  commentary about modern internet culture  protagonists locksley broadcast has  simulated heist a thousand  followers and his growing popularity is  a clear examination of let's play videos  that have come to dominate YouTube  culture but volume never seems to say  anything in the process its story is  disjointed with some characters only  present for dozens of seconds before  being pushed back behind the curtain I  don't see the deposed Queen I don't see  silences I try to warn you the cutscenes  also feel force and I would rather the  developer avoid a story altogether it  often got in the way of the gameplay  with subtitles obscuring important  information before I turn them off  characters also repeated monologues ad  nauseam at checkpoints and their  constant chatter removed me from the  tense stealth game I was trying to focus  on and it is fantastic  there's actual cooldown toys people  still say but when you're able to avoid  the barrier that the overarching  narrative creates volume flows from one  level to the next with the aptitude of a  great stealth game and the inventiveness  of a clever puzzle title

